issue_context.body:
Minimal reproduction
```C#
using System;
using System.Text.Json;
using System.Text.Json.Serialization;
using System.Text.Json.Serialization.Metadata;

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions { TypeInfoResolver = JsonTypeInfoResolver.Combine(MyContext.Default) };
Console.WriteLine(JsonSerializer.Serialize(new MyPoco { Value = 42 }, options));

[JsonSerializable(typeof(MyPoco), GenerationMode = JsonSourceGenerationMode.Serialization)]
public partial class MyContext : JsonSerializerContext
{ }

public class MyPoco
{
    public int Value { get; set; }
}
```
Throws
```
Unhandled exception. System.InvalidOperationException: 'JsonSerializerContext' '<null>' did not provide property metadata for type 'MyPoco'.
   at System.Text.Json.ThrowHelper.ThrowInvalidOperationException_NoMetadataForTypeProperties(JsonSerializerContext context, Type type)
   at System.Text.Json.Serialization.Metadata.SourceGenJsonTypeInfo`1.AddPropertiesUsingSourceGenInfo()
   at System.Text.Json.Serialization.Metadata.JsonTypeInfo.Configure()
   at System.Text.Json.Serialization.Metadata.JsonTypeInfo.EnsureConfigured()
   at System.Text.Json.JsonSerializerOptions.GetOrAddJsonTypeInfo(Type type)
   at System.Text.Json.JsonSerializer.GetTypeInfo(JsonSerializerOptions options, Type runtimeType)
   at System.Text.Json.JsonSerializer.Serialize[TValue](TValue value, JsonSerializerOptions options)
```
This should not throw during the configuration stage, since this is a valid representation of `JsonTypeInfo`. It should support serialization for root-level values of type MyPoco, but should throw an exception when serializing nested values of type `MyPoco` or when deserializing.
